% references.bib — Phase 1 workshop paper
%
% Built at P7 (2026-07-28). Every entry below was cross-verified against two
% independent sources before being written; the queries, the exact source URLs,
% and what each source confirmed are in
% papers/phase1-workshop/runs/20260728T102014Z-P7/search-traces/, one file per
% line of related work, plus an adversarial re-check over a 20% sample.
%
% THE RULE THIS FILE IS UNDER. A record that could not be confirmed twice is not
% here. Where a work has no citable venue, the entry is @misc and says so; no
% arXiv id, DOI, volume or page range appears in this file that was not resolved
% against a source. Do not add an entry by hand without adding its trace.
%
% Known traps, each of which cost a lookup and would otherwise have shipped:
%   * Ha & Schmidhuber is TWO records. "World Models" (1803.10122) was never
%     published under that title; the NeurIPS 2018 paper is 1809.01999 and is
%     titled "Recurrent World Models Facilitate Policy Evolution". A citation
%     reading "World Models, NeurIPS 2018" does not exist.
%   * I-JEPA's own arXiv comment names ICCV. It is CVPR 2023.
%   * DreamerV3 changed title between preprint ("Diverse Domains") and Nature
%     ("diverse control tasks").
%   * Petri 1962 is a TH Darmstadt dissertation. Bonn is the publication locus,
%     not the awarding institution; "University of Bonn" is a widespread error.
%   * AlphaProof's Nature paper does not contain "AlphaProof" in its title, so
%     searching the system name returns nothing and invites invention.
%   * The Dijkstra sentence is EWD249's own wording. The shorter form usually
%     quoted is not what EWD249 says — see dijkstra1970notes.
%
% AUTHOR-NAME CONVENTION. Where sources disagree on the form of a personal name,
% this file follows the PROCEEDINGS OF RECORD — the venue whose volume, pages and
% DOI the entry cites. Aggregators are not authoritative for name spelling:
% Crossref ASCII-folds some diacritics (Bodík -> Bodik) and abbreviates some
% given names, and DBLP ASCII-folds too (Dumančić -> Dumancic). Two entries were
% changed under this rule after the adversarial pass: hao2023rap (the entry cites
% the EMNLP proceedings, so the ACL Anthology's "Joshua Hong" / "Daisy Wang"
% replace arXiv's longer forms) and bruce2024genie (PMLR's "Sarah Maria
% Elisabeth Bechtle" and "De Freitas" replace the shorter arXiv/DBLP forms).
%
% DO NOT "CORRECT" THESE. Both look like errors and are not:
%   * trinh2024alphageometry's DOI reads 10.1038/s41586-*023*-06747-5 on a 2024
%     paper. Nature DOIs carry the submission-year stamp. It resolves.
%   * muggleton1994ilptheory's volume is *19--20*. That is a genuine combined
%     double volume, not a mistyped page range.
%
% FIVE ENTRIES ARE PRESENT BUT UNCITED, deliberately: beasley1992pegsolitaire,
% cropper2021popper, evans2018dilp, hubert2026alphaproof, trinh2024alphageometry.
% They were confirmed to the same standard as the rest and are kept because they
% are the obvious next citations if a section is allowed to run longer. They are
% not orphans and should not be pruned as such.
%
% ONE RECORD IS CONFIRMED TO SECONDARY-SOURCE STANDARD ONLY. openai.com returns
% 403 to automated fetching, so brooks2024sora's 13-name contributor list was
% confirmed from independent scholarly bibliographies rather than from the page
% itself. Whoever finalises this file should open it in a browser once. Its
% publication date (15 Feb 2024) is single-source and is therefore not asserted
% in the entry.

